From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:00:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reserve a block's item list for all its children

The display:none filter hides the length from collect, which then grew the list by doubling; the child count is an upper bound, so a block with many children allocates once. The function is now kept out of line: inlined into the recursive block layout, its locals grew every nesting level's frame, and nested blocks overflowed wasm32's 1 MiB stack about 25 levels sooner.

Signed-off-by: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
---
 src/compute/block.rs | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/compute/block.rs b/src/compute/block.rs
index 261162a..bd819dc 100644
--- a/src/compute/block.rs
+++ b/src/compute/block.rs
@@ -880,13 +880,19 @@ fn compute_inner(
 }

 /// Create a `Vec` of `BlockItem` structs where each item in the `Vec` represents a child of the current node
-#[inline]
+// Kept out of line: inlined, its locals join the frame of the recursive block layout, and on
+// wasm32's 1 MiB stack nested blocks then overflow about 25 levels sooner.
+#[inline(never)]
 fn generate_item_list(
     tree: &impl LayoutBlockContainer,
     node: NodeId,
     node_inner_size: Size<Option<f32>>,
 ) -> Vec<BlockItem> {
-    tree.child_ids(node)
+    // The display:none filter hides the length from the iterator, so an unreserved `Vec` would
+    // grow by doubling: reserve the child count, an upper bound, so a block with many children
+    // allocates once.
+    let mut items = Vec::with_capacity(tree.child_count(node));
+    let children = tree.child_ids(node)
         .map(|child_node_id| (child_node_id, tree.get_block_child_style(child_node_id)))
         .filter(|(_, style)| style.box_generation_mode() != BoxGenerationMode::None)
         .enumerate()
@@ -972,8 +978,9 @@ fn generate_item_list(
                 location: None,
                 oof_candidates: OofCandidates::new(),
             }
-        })
-        .collect()
+        });
+    items.extend(children);
+    items
 }

 /// Resolve the `stretch` sizing keyword for an item's height style. In the block axis the
